        "title": "fix(repair): close staged proof review gaps",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nThis draft hardens ClawSweeper's staged proof, comment-router, and repair requeue paths while keeping mutation safety fail-closed.\n\nThe latest follow-up resolves all four exact-head review findings:\n\n1. exact-item routes persist every selected command before fanout; worker dispatch is serialized through an input-independent durable queue drainer, so GitHub replacing a pending dispatcher cannot replace queued items\n2. broad pagination reserves actionable, unprocessed command comments rather than each item's newest unrelated comment\n3. every broad continuation carries the same effective `since` captured in the first route report\n4. `requeue=true` requires authenticated one-shot context and a deterministic bounded dispatch key, and fails closed when either is absent or unstable\n\nThe durable dispatcher groups duplicate item/comment work, retains each command's branch, runner, scan timestamp, forced-replay identity, and status-comment ID, and waits at the serialized live-worker capacity gate before dispatch.\n\nThe PR also includes the staged-proof ceiling, traversal, retry, strict-base, autoclose hydration, forced replay, pagination, and GitHub API/query-bound hardening from the earlier repair passes.\n\n## Queue blocker resolved\n\nExact routing remains item-keyed. Selected commands are first committed to `results/comment-router.json`, then a shared dispatcher drains all waiting or claimed commands for the target repository. The dispatcher does not depend on the exact item that happened to trigger its run, so GitHub Actions' single-pending concurrency behavior can coalesce dispatcher runs without dropping durable work.\n\n## Latest repair commit\n\n- `32858a0c52` `fix(router): preserve queued routing progress`\n\n## Validation\n\n- exact head: `32858a0c5255142a0901cfb2efcf05f33cb9ffc8`\n- exact tree: `663eb4a9b9d5e3ec03b52d8980d5bcee7ff7c51d`\n- rebased merge base: `9a859325116cc55545b2bf1a0578685136ec081d`\n- Node: `v26.5.0`\n- focused router, pagination, requeue, strict-binding, and workflow suite: `343/343`\n- full `pnpm --config.verify-deps-before-run=false run check`: passed on the exact tree\n  - unit: `1089` passed, `2` skipped, `0` failed\n  - repair: `946/946`\n  - changed coverage: `100.00%` lines, `86.90%` branches, `100.00%` functions\n  - aggregate coverage: `74.52%` lines, `73.65%` branches, `84.66%` functions\n  - builds, lint, active-surface/limit checks, and formatting over `362` files passed\n- `git diff --check`: passed\n\nThe PR remains draft and unmerged.\n",
